From 0696b0a32e850e7e7b06bc089a8ff6052158fdad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CipherScope <dev@cipherscope.io>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 23:34:33 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 61/65] test: add unit tests for the P2MR tripwire parameters,
 options and state

p2mr_tripwire_tests checks:

- the heights and tripwire outputs of each network: none yet on Ark-0,
  never on the other signets, the testnets and mainnet without the
  option, and genesis without tripwire outputs on regtest unless
  -testactivationheight moves it;
- -signetmldsa44 and -signettripwire on a custom signet, with the log of
  the rules, and every way they are refused: without -signetchallenge,
  on Ark-0, without -signetmldsa44 or at or below its height, with a
  malformed value, height 0 or an outpoint named twice;
- -signettripwire on regtest, which -testactivationheight=p2mr_tripwire
  cannot accompany and which needs the p2mr_mldsa44 height below it;
- -signetmldsa44 on mainnet, the testnets and regtest, and
  -signettripwire on mainnet and the testnets, refused whatever their
  value;
- which outputs are present and whether elliptic curve checks fail in
  the next block: an output never created, created below the height,
  spent, created again at the height, and created again below it; and
  never without tripwire outputs;
- that ConnectBlock reads the state from the view it is given, the UTXO
  set the block builds on, as the background chainstate of an assumeutxo
  snapshot needs: a block with a Schnorr spend of a 0xe0 leaf is valid on
  a view where the tripwire output is present, and invalid on the active
  chain's, where it is missing.
